{
  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on the presence of a sure outcome (i.e., an outcome with 100% probability) in each lottery. A sure outcome is one that will definitely occur, regardless of chance. In Lottery A, no outcome occurs with 100% probability: 4000 Euros has 25%, 2000 Euros has 25%, and 0 Euros has 50%. In Lottery B, 0 Euros occurs with 75% probability and 6000 Euros with 25%; thus, no outcome is certain. Therefore, neither lottery contains a sure outcome. The decision reason would be indifferent between the two lotteries, as neither has a sure outcome. The relevant information for the reason is that both lotteries are uncertain, with no deterministic payoffs.",
